---
description: Active engine and client/server authority boundary
alwaysApply: true
---

- The active in-round gameplay engine is **Phaser 3 + TypeScript** under `client/src/game/`.
  React owns landing, lobby, intros, leaderboard, winner and modal/accessibility overlays.
- `client/src/game/GameEventBridge.ts` is the only React/network ↔ Phaser boundary. Phaser
  consumes snapshots and emits intents; scenes never import sockets or Zustand.
- Phaser code in `experiments/loot-drop/` remains archived reference. Do not import its stale
  socket contract or standalone server.
- The server (`server/src/engine.ts`) is authoritative. Phaser/React render public/private
  state and send intents; neither computes correct answers, random outcomes or score mutations.
- Shared pure logic belongs in `shared/src/game/`; named values belong in `shared/src/config/`;
  socket/state types belong in `shared/src/types/index.ts`.
- Animation timelines must tolerate late/out-of-order state, cancel on phase/question changes
  and reconstruct from current state after reconnect.
- `PhaserGame.tsx` owns canvas lifecycle only; game state lives in the bridge/server.
- Canonical architecture: `docs/context/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
